{
  "_comment": "Strictest default-deny seccomp profile for the UNTRUSTED agent-runtime / test-runtime sandbox (Plan 15 task_15_15, ADR 0012). This container runs hostile-by-assumption agent/test code, so its allowlist is a strict subset of default.json: it lets a Python/Node/PHP process compute, do file I/O inside its read-only-root + tmpfs workspace, and talk to the egress proxy, but it does NOT allow the namespace/privilege/kernel-module/tracing family. Every dangerous syscall (mount, umount2, ptrace, process_vm_readv, process_vm_writev, kexec_load, kexec_file_load, bpf, init_module, finit_module, delete_module, reboot, swapon, swapoff, pivot_root, chroot, setns, unshare, keyctl, add_key, request_key, mount_setattr, open_by_handle_at, name_to_handle_at, perf_event_open, acct, settimeofday, clock_settime, stime, vhangup, nfsservctl, quotactl) is deliberately ABSENT from the allowlist, so defaultAction SCMP_ACT_ERRNO rejects it. clone is allowed WITHOUT namespace flags only (CLONE_NEW* is filtered by the no-new-privileges + cap_drop ALL envelope; this profile additionally argues the syscall surface). Loaded by workers.isolation.build_hardened_run_kwargs (WORKERS_SECCOMP_PROFILE) which forwards the profile CONTENT to the daemon.",
